SUMMARY:The Lancaster Living Poetry Museum II
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster will celebrate National Poetry Month by preparing for The Lancaster Living Poetry Museum II.  On Saturday\, May 2\, all performers will be on stage at Zoetropolis Cinema Still House in a full-cast show at 7:00 pm. Tickets are available on Zoetropolis’ website. This event is an initiative founded and directed by Lancaster City Poet Laureate Dana Kinsey. \n\n\n\nThe following performers will bring poets to life: Carol Allen as Shakespeare\, PAN as Amelia Earhart\, Lee Morr as Shel Silverstein\, and Coral Rites and sean poets as Andrea Gibson\, Maria Thompson-Corley as Lucille Clifton\, Malia Burris as Noʻu Revilla\, Bronte Spidaliere as Louise Glück\, Ruel Rahim as Fela Aníkúlápó Kuti\, Beimnet Getahun as Hiwot Adilow\, Circumstantial Saint as Langston Hughes\, Dana Kinsey as Edna St. Vincent Millay\, Natalie Knox as Elizabeth Barrett Browning\, Sir Dominique Jordan as Muhammad Ali\, Starr Snyder as Jewel\, Ángel Rafael as Miguel Piñero\, and Shelby Wormley as India Arie.  
URL:https://visitlancastercity.com/event/the-lancaster-living-poetry-museum-ii-2/
LOCATION:Zoetropolis Cinema Stillhouse\, 112 North Water Street\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17063\, United States
CATEGORIES:Arts and Culture,History
END:VEVENT
